"""
pdf_autofill.py -- generate a filled assignment contract for a Deal.

Inputs:
  - Deal UUID (from Django)  OR an ad-hoc dict via --json
  - Optional override of buyer/escrow info

Outputs:
  /home/opc/wholesale_agent/contracts_out/<deal_id>/
    - assignment.md     (filled markdown, easy to read)
    - assignment.html   (filled HTML, what gets sent to HelloSign)
    - assignment.pdf    (filled PDF, for manual sign or attachment)

Placeholder convention: the template uses [SQUARE_BRACKET] tokens. We map
each token to a value pulled from the Deal/PropertyLead/InvestorBuyer chain
or from a constants block. Unknown tokens get flagged so we never ship a
contract with a bracket still in it.

State-aware: the [STATE_EMD_RULES] block fills with state-specific text
(CA / OH / GA / TX) so the contract is jurisdictionally correct.

Usage:
  python3 pdf_autofill.py --deal-id <uuid>
  python3 pdf_autofill.py --json '{"address":"123 Main St", ...}'  # ad-hoc
  python3 pdf_autofill.py --dry-run --deal-id <uuid>               # log unmapped tokens

Once DOCUMENSO_API_KEY is in env (token from https://sign.everlightventures.io/settings/tokens),
this script ALSO posts the signature request to self-hosted Documenso and
updates Deal.agreement_url. Until the key is set, it stops at the file-write
step. Documenso replaces the original HelloSign integration: same legal
posture (ESIGN + UETA compliant, court-admissible audit trail), zero monthly
cost, data stays on Oracle.
"""

